hed from this legacy research implementation. MIT applies to project code; external libraries keep their own terms.", "published_at": null, "relations": [{"evidence_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sikuli/sikuli/HEAD/docs/source/index.rst", "target_id": "url:a4cdb2ee0d07d3980651", "type": "documented_by"}, {"evidence_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sikuli/sikuli/HEAD/docs/source/index.rst", "target_id": "url:6262c757080f8838e62c", "type": "documented_by"}], "review_status": "curated", "scope": "core", "summary": "The original Sikuli source distribution combines screenshot targets with a Jython scripting library and IDE for visual GUI automation and testing.", "topics": ["automation", "grounding", "screen-understanding", "history"], "updated_at": null, "url": "https://github.com/sikuli/sikuli"}
